  "summary": "Adversaries increasingly abuse signed, legitimate remote monitoring and management (RMM) tools as loaders and persistence mechanisms, often chaining two or more RMMs on one host and using MSIExec to break process lineage. Detection should focus on renamed installers, tool-specific metadata/User-Agents, config files and tokens, RMM binaries spawning other RMMs, and newly registered C2 domains embedded in command lines. This profile captures the per-tool file, process, command-line, and network artifacts Red Canary identifies as the highest-fidelity detection anchors.",
